# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# NOTE: the patterns must stand alone on their line. An inline trailing comment
# is NOT a comment in .gitignore — it becomes part of the pattern, so a line like
# "config/api_keys.json   # my key" matches no file at all and silently publishes
# the secret. Keep explanations on their own lines above the pattern.
#
# config/api_keys.json     — the Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
# config/certs/            — the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
# config/whatsapp_web/     — a LINKED WhatsApp session; committing it hands
#                            somebody your WhatsApp account, not just a key
# **/token*.json           — Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
# **/client_secret*.json   — Google OAuth client secrets
config/api_keys.json
config/certs/
config/whatsapp_web/
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
# The app's stores are SQLite and are named *.sqlite3, NOT *.db — without these
# lines the telemetry and OSINT databases (megabytes, full conversation history)
# get committed by any fresh `git add .`.
memory/*.sqlite3
memory/*.sqlite3-shm
memory/*.sqlite3-wal

# ── Local backups of edited files (editors and manual copies) ────────────────
backups/
*.bak
scratch/

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Vendored third-party tools ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `vendor/` holds full external projects checked out next to ours (deep-eye and
# friends) together with their own virtualenvs. They carry their own history,
# their own .gitignore and tens of thousands of lines we did not write.
#
# They must NOT be committed:
#   * `git pull` in vendor/deep-eye is how the tool gets updated, and a commit
#     of its contents would make that a merge conflict instead.
#   * Its data/ dir holds scan results, auth sessions and a RAG index — real
#     findings about real hosts, i.e. exactly the kind of thing that should not
#     live in a repository.
#
# The pattern stands alone on its line; an inline trailing comment would become
# part of the pattern and silently match nothing (see the note above).
vendor/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
# deep-eye keeps its own interpreter next to the JARVIS one, deliberately:
# it pins google-genai>=0.8 while JARVIS needs >=2.8,<3, and sharing the venv
# would break Gemini Live.
.deep-venv/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
